\ql\fs20\par
\f1 IMPORTANT\f0\par
Read these terms before installing or using Abdullah Properties Office, the Application. By installing, accessing, or using the Application, you confirm that you are an authorised Abdullah Properties staff member or contractor and that you accept these terms. If you are not authorised or do not accept them, do not install or use the Application.\par
\par
This document is an operational draft for installer review. It is not legal advice. Abdullah Properties must obtain appropriate legal review and confirm the governing-law clause before approving a production release.\par
\par
\f1 1. APPLICATION AND LICENSE SCOPE\f0\par
Abdullah Properties grants authorised staff and approved contractors a limited, non-exclusive, non-transferable, revocable right to install and use the Application on approved Windows devices solely for Abdullah Properties office work. The Application is not licensed for public, customer, resale, hosting, sublicensing, or unrelated commercial use. No ownership is transferred. The Abdullah Properties name, marks, interface, written material, and original application material remain the property of Abdullah Properties or their identified owners and may be used only as authorised.\par
\par
\f1 2. AUTHORISED USE AND ACCESS\f0\par
Use only your own approved Windows account and paired office device. Follow assigned roles, permissions, office procedures, and signed commercial documents. Provide accurate, lawful information and verify records before relying on them. Lock the device when unattended and promptly report loss, theft, suspected compromise, or unauthorised access. Stop using the Application when access expires, is revoked, or your work authorisation ends.\par
\par
Do not share a device credential, copy it into messages or screenshots, bypass a permission or security control, probe the service, introduce malicious code, alter records without authority, or use the Application to misrepresent an approval, payment, delivery, ownership position, or contractual commitment.\par
\par
\f1 3. LOCAL, OFFLINE, AND PROVISIONAL RECORDS\f0\par
The Application is offline-first. It can retain form autosaves, local drafts, provisional payment acknowledgements, and queued operations in an application-local SQLite database. Browser preview storage is for development only and is not the native production data store.\par
\par
Offline or queued content is not an authoritative server record. Network availability does not prove that a record has synchronized. Only a validated acknowledgement from the Abdullah Properties server may mark an eligible operation as accepted or synchronized.\par
\par
The current synchronization boundary accepts creates for leads, invoice drafts, and notice drafts. It does not pull authoritative changes or edit a server-accepted draft. Conflicts, rejected operations, expired credentials, and permission failures must be reviewed instead of being treated as completed work.\par
\par
\f1 4. FINANCIAL AND DOCUMENT BOUNDARY\f0\par
The Application does not by itself allocate an official invoice, receipt, or notice number; post or allocate a payment; change an authoritative balance; complete finance reconciliation; reserve or transfer a property; approve a transaction; send an email, SMS, push, or in-application notification; or prove that a document was delivered, received, paid, accepted, or approved.\par
\par
Every printable offline document must remain visibly marked PROVISIONAL or LOCAL. Printing, exporting to PDF, saving, or seeing an internet connection does not change that status. Official records and customer communications require the applicable hosted-server acceptance, authorised staff review, verified numbering, audit record, and approved delivery process. Separate signed documents govern property, development, joint-venture, consultancy, payment, and other commercial engagements.\par
\par
\f1 5. CREDENTIAL AND DEVICE SECURITY\f0\par
The Application protects its paired-device bearer credential with Windows Data Protection for the current Windows user. This protection does not replace a secured Windows account, device access controls, approved full-disk protection, patching, malware protection, or incident response.\par
\par
The local SQLite database is not automatically encrypted by the Application. Do not store payment-card data, passwords, unnecessary identity documents, or other information that has not been approved for local processing. Do not copy the database, logs, exports, or credentials to personal storage, unapproved cloud services, consumer messaging services, or removable media. Device credentials are revocable, may expire, and grant only their assigned permissions.\par
\par
\f1 6. PRIVACY AND CONFIDENTIALITY\f0\par
Office, customer, property, financial, contact, and project information must be treated as confidential and handled only for a lawful, authorised business purpose. Collect only information that is reasonably needed. Verify recipients and attachments before using an external email, telephone, WhatsApp, printing, or other service. Third-party services operate under their own security and privacy terms. Follow applicable Abdullah Properties privacy, retention, access, incident, and deletion procedures, applicable law, and signed confidentiality obligations. Report a suspected privacy or security incident through the approved office process without delay.\par
\par
\f1 7. BACKUPS, RETENTION, AND RECOVERY\f0\par
Synchronization is not a complete backup. Abdullah Properties is responsible for approving backup locations, retention periods, encryption, access, recovery procedures, and deletion. Users must not create informal or personal backups. Before an upgrade, repair, reset, or uninstall, follow the approved backup and recovery procedure. A production release must be tested for clean installation, upgrade, rollback, uninstall, migration, crash recovery, and preservation or intentional removal of local data. Recovery capability should be tested, not assumed.\par
\par
\f1 8. UPDATES AND SUPPORTED VERSIONS\f0\par
Install updates only from an approved Abdullah Properties distribution channel. A release must not be treated as trusted merely because it has a familiar file name or logo. Verify its published source and, for a production build, its digital signature and release information. Updates may change compatibility, security controls, data migrations, and supported workflows. Abdullah Properties may require an update or withdraw an obsolete or vulnerable version. Do not downgrade, replace, or modify the Application outside an approved recovery process.\par
\par
\f1 9. AVAILABILITY AND DISCLAIMER\f0\par
The Application is provided for authorised office operations and may be changed, suspended, or unavailable for maintenance, security, provider failure, network failure, or circumstances outside reasonable control. No software, device, network, backup, or security control can be guaranteed error-free or continuously available. To the extent permitted by applicable law, Abdullah Properties does not warrant that the Application will prevent every data loss, security incident, duplicate, conflict, delay, or user error. Users remain responsible for review, verification, and compliance with approved office procedures. Nothing in these terms excludes a responsibility that cannot lawfully be excluded.\par
\par
\f1 10. LIMITATION OF LIABILITY\f0\par
To the extent permitted by applicable law, Abdullah Properties is not responsible for loss caused solely by unauthorised use, an unapproved device or backup, reliance on a provisional or unconfirmed record, an external service, bypassed controls, or an event outside reasonable control. Rights and remedies in an applicable signed agreement remain subject to that agreement.\par
\par
\f1 11. TERMINATION\f0\par
This license ends automatically when your authorisation ends or when you materially breach these terms. Abdullah Properties may also revoke access or require removal for security, operational, or legal reasons. On termination, stop using the Application, return or protect business records as directed, remove unauthorised copies, and do not delete records that must be preserved under an approved retention or legal-hold process.\par
